 payment-api; checkout-web recorded payment-api auth_failed with invalid issuer while static assets recovered normally.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"The database reported normal 35 ms query latency and zero errors; no failed checkout transaction reached it because requests stopped at the auth gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge HTTP 5xx rate of 4.8%\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"The metric notes the errors were isolated to images, and checkout-web confirmed static assets served normally after retry while checkout remained blocked. CDN is not on the payment authorization dependency path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"checkout-web elevated latency\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"This is a downstream symptom of rejected/failed payment authorization, not evidence of an independent checkout-web fault.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n    \"Immediately halt or roll back AUTH-2026-0318, or restore partner-v2 in auth-gateway allowed_issuers using the approved change process.\",\n    \"Repair and invalidate/rebuild the JWKS cache under the intended partner-v2 namespace, then confirm token validation succeeds.\",\n    \"Run a controlled checkout payment authorization and verify a successful payment-api response and downstream order creation.\",\n    \"Monitor HTTP 401 rates and p95 latency for auth-gateway, payment-api, and checkout-web until they return to baseline; separately track CDN image errors and orders-db CPU.\"\n  ]\n}\n"}}}}
