ence","content":"Inspect topology metrics and service logs"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788158628739},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522a6f8d087d28ec58306feff22fb\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"0df59c24-f4e0-44ad-b6c6-fdc16287167d\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"0df59c24-f4e0-44ad-b6c6-fdc16287167d\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_l1mwP9fP2NRAZfVyVdnL2qCs|fc_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522a7c93887d28c99a7b97141682e","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write root cause report","path":"out/root_cause.json","content":"{\n  \"incident_id\": \"checkout-service-dependency-2026-03-22\",\n  \"root_cause_service\": \"auth-gateway\",\n  \"root_cause_change_id\": \"AUTH-2026-0318\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"affected_services\": [\n    \"checkout-web\",\n    \"payment-api\",\n    \"auth-gateway\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"in/topology.json\",\n      \"observation\": \"The checkout-web dependency path includes payment-api, which depends on auth-gateway; AUTH-2026-0318 is the recent auth-gateway change and rotated the issuer and JWKS cache namespace.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n      \"observation\": \"At 14:10Z, checkout-web had an 18.7% HTTP 401 rate and 2400 ms p95 with checkout submits rejected after payment auth; payment-api had a 21.2% 401 rate and notes an invalid issuer; auth-gateway had a 28.4% 401 rate and issuer mismatch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"AUTH-2026-0318 deployed at 14:05Z; auth-gateway then logged a JWKS cache miss and rejected token issuer partner-v2 because only partner-v1 was allowed. The log explicitly identifies restoring partner-v2 or reverting AUTH-2026-0318 as rollback candidates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"in/logs/payment-api.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"Payment token validation failed upstream at auth-gateway with issuer_not_allowed for partner-v2, and request req-8812 was rejected as invalid_issuer before the order-db dependency was used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"Checkout submit req-8812 failed with a 401 from payment-api; checkout-web recorded payment-api auth_failed with invalid issuer while static assets recovered normally.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"The database reported normal 35 ms query latency and zero errors; no failed checkout transaction reached it because requests stopped at the auth gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge HTTP 5xx rate of 4.8%\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"The metric notes the errors were isolated to images, and checkout-web confirmed static assets served normally after retry while checkout remained blocked. CDN is not on the payment authorization dependency path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"checkout-web elevated latency\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"This is a downstream symptom of rejected/failed payment authorization, not evidence of an independent checkout-web fault.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n    \"Immediately halt or roll back AUTH-2026-0318, or restore partner-v2 in auth-gateway allowed_issuers using the approved change process.\",\n    \"Repair and invalidate/rebuild the JWKS cache under the intended partner-v2 namespace, then confirm token validation succeeds.\",\n    \"Run a controlled checkout payment authorization and verify a successful payment-api response and downstream order creation.\",\n    \"Monitor HTTP 401 rates and p95 latency for auth-gateway, payment-api, and checkout-web until they return to baseline; separately track CDN image errors and orders-db CPU.\"\n  ]\n}\n"},"intent":"Write root cause report"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":550,"output":890,"cacheRead":18176,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19616,"reasoningTokens":37,"cost":{"input":0.00011,"output":0.001068,"cacheRead":0.00036352,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00154152}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788158628770,"responseId":"resp_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522a5097887d2a4b2f56fb7dae113","duration":18253.253705000003,"ttft":2236.772589},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_l1mwP9fP2NRAZfVyVdnL2qCs|fc_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522a7c93887d28c99a7b97141682e","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/root_cause.json#91A5]\nSuccessfully wrote 3126 bytes to out/root_cause.json"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/root_cause.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788158647056},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_fgWkFTfKI0GXhFrgvZ7BEbqY|fc_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522b7eb7087d2be043a3c526c7011","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write triage notes","path":"out/triage_notes.md","content":"# Checkout dependency triage\n\n## Conclusion\n\n**Root cause: `auth-gateway`, change `AUTH-2026-0318` (high confidence).** The change deployed at 14:05Z and introduced an issuer/JWKS namespace mismatch: tokens carrying issuer `partner-v2` were rejected because the configured allowed issuer remained `partner-v1`.\n\n## Dependency path\n\nThe user-facing path is:\n\n`checkout-web` → `payment-api` → `auth-gateway`\n\nThis path is directly defined in `in/topology.json`. At 14:09:41Z, `checkout-web` logged `submit_order` failing with HTTP 401 from `payment-api` (`in/logs/checkout-web.log`). `payment-api` then recorded that validation failed upstream at `auth-gateway` with `issuer_not_allowed` for `partner-v2`, and rejected the payment request as `invalid_issuer` (`in/logs/payment-api.log`). `auth-gateway` recorded the deployment, JWKS cache miss, and the decisive mismatch—`token_issuer=partner-v2` versus `allowed_issuers=partner-v1`—in `in/logs/auth-gateway.log`.\n\nThe metrics corroborate the same chain: at 14:10Z, HTTP 401 rates were 18.7% for `checkout-web`, 21.2% for `payment-api`, and 28.4% for `auth-gateway`; the corresponding notes identify rejected checkout submits, invalid issuer responses, and issuer mismatch (`in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`).\n\n**Directly observed facts:** the dependency edges, deployment/change ID, log messages, issuer values, allowed issuer, request rejection, and 14:10Z metric values stated above are present in the cited fixtures.\n\n**Inference:** the issuer configuration/cache namespace behavior introduced by `AUTH-2026-0318` is the primary causal fault because it precedes and explains the correlated 401s across the dependency path. The fixture evidence supports this with high confidence, but does not show the change diff itself.\n\n## Misleading signals\n\n- `orders-db` CPU reached 86%, but `in/metrics/service_metrics.csv` shows normal 35 ms query latency and zero errors. `in/logs/orders-db.log` says the failing request never reached the database. This is maintenance-related, not the checkout blocker.\n- `cdn-edge` showed 4.8% HTTP 5xx, but the metric limits the issue to images. `in/logs/checkout-web.log` says static assets recovered while checkout remained blocked, and CDN is not on the payment authorization path.\n- Elevated checkout latency is a downstream symptom of failed payment authorization, not a separate root cause.\n\n## Immediate mitigation\n\n1. Halt or roll back `AUTH-2026-0318`, **or** restore `partner-v2` to `allowed_issuers`, following the approved emergency-change process.\n2. Invalidate/rebuild the JWKS cache for the intended `partner-v2` namespace.\n3. Avoid retry storms while authorization is failing; preserve representative request IDs such as `req-8812` for correlation.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Submit a controlled checkout payment authorization and confirm `auth-gateway` accepts a `partner-v2` token.\n2. Confirm `payment-api` returns success and the request proceeds to order creation; this must be a new controlled transaction because the failing fixture request stopped before `orders-db`.\n3. Confirm HTTP 401 rates and p95 latency for `auth-gateway`, `payment-api`, and `checkout-web` return toward the baseline shown in `in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`.\n4. Verify no new `invalid_issuer` or `issuer_not_allowed` entries appear in the three service logs during the observation window. Track the independent CDN image errors and database CPU separately.\n"},"intent":"Write triage notes"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1472,"output":852,"cacheRead":18176,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20500,"cost":{"input":0.0002944,"output":0.0010224,"cacheRead":0.00036352,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00168032}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788158647058,"responseId":"resp_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522b75aac87d2b66ce1b80c3a5042","duration":16168.639127000002,"ttft":895.1233950000023},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_fgWkFTfKI0GXhFrgvZ7BEbqY|fc_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522b7eb7087d2be043a3c526c7011","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/triage_notes.md#963E]\nSuccessfully wrote 3428 bytes to out/triage_notes.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/triage_notes.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788158663235},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522c7e99487d2b6b6b4c31c7d5a01\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"0df59c24-f4e0-44ad-b6c6-fdc16287167d\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"0df59c24-f4e0-44ad-b6c6-fdc16287167d\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_kYSLO4cSZYJivY14eXsKBw68|fc_0c028ebe0f46f021016a9522c8fd2887d2a04aa9b102395e40","name":"tod